{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see! Now I understand the pattern better.\n\nIn the comments feature:\n1. `create-comment.ts` and `delete-comment.ts` API hooks use `getInfiniteCommentsQueryOptions(discussionId).queryKey` in `invalidateQueries` - this is correct (using query options function)\n2. `get-comments.ts` has `getInfiniteCommentsQueryOptions` which returns `infiniteQueryOptions` with `queryKey: ['comments', discussionId]`. Here the literal key array `['comments', discussionId]` is inside `infiniteQueryOptions()`, which is ALLOWED per the rule.\n\nThe components (`create-comment.tsx` and `delete-comment.tsx` in components folder) are USING `useNotifications` - this is VIOLATING the rule.\n\nNow let me check the discussions feature:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_vseuyhw6","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/components/create-discussion.tsx"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_u1nric89","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/components/delete-discussion.tsx"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8gjovz5g","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/components/update-discussion.tsx"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.6:35b-a3b-coding","usage":{"input":941,"output":288,"cacheRead":9980,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":11209,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793787812844,"responseId":"chatcmpl-935","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":5590,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_vseuyhw6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { Plus } from 'lucide-react';\n\nimport { Button } from '@/components/ui/button';\nimport { Form, FormDrawer, Input, Textarea } from '@/components/ui